							<p><span class="title"><strong><font face="Arial" size="2">CHARTER /RULES</font></strong></span> </p> <p> <hr size="1" /> <p></p> <p>Inverse Logic is family-oriented guild that focuses on the excitement and challenge that exist on Norrath. We are a group of honest and caring individuals that work closely together towards the betterment of each other as a whole. <br /><br />Below are the rules that each guild member must abide by.<br /><br />--Above all else treat your fellow members as you would like to be treated. Members that are abusive, obnoxious, or generally disruptive may be removed from the guild at anytime without notice. They are permitted to contest the removal.<br /><br />--Disruption will not be tolerated on the Guild Channel. This includes buying/selling/trading items and any other conversations that could be brought to private tells. Profane or offensive language in guild chat will not be tolerated as it is also disruptive. The Guild channel is best suited for important conversations so that it doesn't constantly spam (or offend) members. <br /><br />--IL members are not to be botted by anyone outside of the guild. If this causes some kind of complication, please discuss it with an officer or Zentix to see if some compromise can be reached.<br /><br />--On Guild Raids casters that use spell components are to be compensated through the guild fund. All coins and items that will be sold for coins will be turned in to the guild fund to help cover the costs of the raids.<br /><br />--Officers and raidleaders are extensions of the Guild Leader and are to be treated with respect at ALL times. Disrespecting them could result in a warning or guildremoval. <br /><br />--Begging is not tolerated, in guildchat or through tells. Continually spamming guildchat with requests for help is both inconsiderate and counterproductive. Members will give reasonable assistance to fellow members, but will not be required to assist in endeavors detrimental to their person or belongings, nor to provide items or money to other members except of their own free will. Leaving a group or camp, crossing multiple zones, paying costs out of pocket, or leaving a guild event are all things that could be considered unreasonable.<br /><br />--If you, as a member, decide to apply to another guild, please remove your IL guild tag before doing so. It is considered rude and bad form to continue to hold the IL tag while applying to join another guild. If you do not remove your tag an officer will ask you to or help you in doing so <!--EZCODE EMOTICON START ;) --><img alt="" src="http://www.ezboard.com/intl/aenglish/images/emoticons/wink.gif" /><!--EZCODE EMOTICON END--> <br /><br />--All upgradable items are rewarded via MERIT determined by the Inverse Logic leadership (guild leader, officers, raidleaders). Particular contributing factors to merit decisions include: the usefulness of the item for a particular class, how often a person raids (raid attendance), how much time has passed since the previous merit, how large an upgrade the item will be, length of time as a member of the guild, etc. Only full members are considered for merited loot. If the item is not droppable, and no full member present would benefit (rot), probation members and invites would be allowed to send requests for the item in question. All droppable items will remain in the guild to upgrade members or replenish the guild fund.<br /><br />3. Multiple Characters: <br />1 acct/ 1 comp: Unless the raid leader specifies your alt would be more useful on the raid than your main, the alts are eligible for loot that no main present will use (rot).<br /><br />2 accts/ 2 comps: The bots have to be lvl 62+ to be considered full member for receiving merited loot, and they must have a particular responsibility on the raid (such as healing, snaring etc). Check with raid leader on whether or not it applies to your bot. If the bot is of necessary level and useful, it will be considered for merit as the primary would. Bots that are not useful or necessary on a raid will not be given attendance points for that raid.<br /><br />2 accts/ 1 comp: Same as for 1 comp/1acct<br />Unless more needed than your main, your alt is eligible for rot loot only. Raidleader/officer must specifically request you play an alt for raid success to be eligible for non-rot loot.<br /><br />If you feel there would be any confusion on who your main and your alts are, talk to an officer about it and make sure its cleared up.<br /><br />5. In the cases where items are rolled upon, the numbers will be chosen at time of /random.<br /><br />6.Epics: There will be NO discussion of epic mobs/raids in guild chat. Coordination of ANY epic work requiring help from guild members that is not guild sponsored must be carried out in tells; NOT through the guild channel.<br /><br />7. Runes will be rolled on by Full Members in attendance ONLY. Spectral parchments will be rolled on by Full and Probation members only. Ethereal parchments can be rolled on by any participant. You must be 61+ to roll for ethereals (can scribe spell), 63+ to roll for spectrals, and 65 for runes. Officers/Raidleaders will loot spectrals/runes and do turn-ins and keep any duplicates in the guild for others in need. /Random numbers are listed above.<br /><br /><br />****These loot rules can be altered on any particular raid if decided upon beforehand by the entire group of participants.****<br /><br /><br /><!--EZCODE BOLD START--><strong>Keep in mind that the Guild Leader has the final say in all matters concerning the guild and will make decisions based on what is best for the guild as a whole.</strong><!--EZCODE BOLD END--> <br /><br />For Members Only:</p> <p><a href="custom.aspx?pid=1189">Official Raid Times</a></p> <p><a href="custom.aspx?pid=1179">Raid rules</a></p> <p><br />&nbsp;</p><!--EZCODE CENTER START--> <div style="TEXT-ALIGN: center">-----Membership----- </div><!--EZCODE CENTER END--> <p><br />Becoming a member of IL is a lengthy process and requires a lot of effort on the part of the prospective member. Seek us out and get in touch with officers so that we can get to know you and have you along on guild events. You will not be able to get in without having made friends in the guild who can sponsor your application.<br /><br />Any person invited for membership must go through a 21 day trial(probationary) period. After the 21 days are finished, all full members can vote on whether or not to invite the probationary member for full membership, decline membership, or extend the trial period for an additional 21 days. Only <!--EZCODE BOLD START--><strong>one</strong><!--EZCODE BOLD END--> additional 21 day trial period can be granted. If at the end of the second period there are still insufficient votes for full membership, the probationary member will be asked to leave, but can reapply at a later time.<br /><br />During the trial period, probationary members are to group and raid with IL as often as possible so that the members can get to know them and see how they fit with the guild. Probationary members will carry guildtag.<br /><br />The 21 day trial period is the time where both the guild and the probation member can determine if the person fits in the guild. It is a critical time used to get to know other members and determine if this is the right guild for you. Do not expect nor demand any large guild effort or support towards personal gains such as quests or gear acquisition. This 21 day period is best used finding your place within the guild, not what you can obtain from it. Gain the support and loyalty of your fellow guildmates upon becoming a full member, and you will more likely receive the help you need. If you feel confident enough about your position in the guild and as a probation member that you would like to request help on a quest or other such things, please resort to tells rather than using the guild channel.<br /><br />For more detailed information, please read the application info found <a href="/custom.aspx?pid=1176">here</a>. If your answer is not found there, get in touch with an officer through a&nbsp;private ezboard message or /tell in game. </p> <p><a href="custom.aspx?pid=1193">Contact List for Officers and Classleaders</a><br /></p>
							
